    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"U4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U4.10\", \"U4.11\", \"U4.12\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On the display sheet, BS0 (pin 10) is wired up to the VCC symbol. BS1 (pin 11) and BS2 (pin 12) are joined together and go to GND. The strapping is therefore BS0=1, BS1=0, BS2=0.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec gives the interface-select strapping as BS0 to GND, BS1 to VCC, BS2 to GND (BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0) for the SSD1306 I2C mode.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`BS0` (pin 10) \u2192 GND; `BS1` (pin 11) \u2192 VCC; `BS2` (pin 12) \u2192 GND. That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch: BS0 pin 10 wire runs to a VCC power symbol; BS1 pin 11 and BS2 pin 12 share a node that connects to a GND symbol\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The SSD1306 is strapped into a different bus mode from the intended I2C mode. The MCU's I2C transactions on DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA will not be recognised and the OLED will not work.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.6\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"missing_component\",\n      \"components\": [\"R4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U4.14\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"DISP_RES\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The display sheet has no R4. DISP_RES connects only to U4 pin 14 (RES#) and a hierarchical label, with no pull-up to VCC.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec states that R4 (10 k\u03a9) pulls DISP_RES up to VCC, holding the active-low RES# high when the MCU does not drive it.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`DISP_RES`: U2 pin 33 (`PB12`) \u2014 R4 (10 k\u03a9) to VCC \u2014 U4 pin 14 (`RES#`), active-low reset held high by R4's pull-up\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch: R5, R6, R7 and C7\u2013C13, C17, C19 are drawn; no resistor is drawn between DISP_RES and VCC\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"RES# is left without a defined idle level if the MCU's PB12 is high-impedance during reset or boot, so the display may reset unpredictably.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The display's BS0/BS1 interface-select straps are swapped relative to the spec's I2C-mode strapping (BS1 should be VCC, BS0 GND), which would stop the OLED from working over I2C. The R4 RES# pull-up described in the spec is also absent from the drawing.\"\n}",
